there's quite a lot of good news about  covered 19 recently but some people have  been pointing towards quite a scary  statistic certainly scary  on the surface and it comes in this  table from public health england looking  at who's got the delta variants and  what's happened to them later on  and i'll just circle it you can see it  there look of those who've received two  doses of the vaccination 224  died in fact actually if you look across  those who have been vaccinated one or  two dose  the majority of those deaths were people  who were vaccinated which raised us a  question are the vaccines  working what's going wrong here well  it's worth just bearing in mind  two things here because actually these  numbers aren't quite as scary as they  look at first the first thing  is that even though these vaccines  should reduce the risk  of death they don't eliminate it now  these bars here show you your mortality  risk so the risk of getting the disease  and dying by age group from youngest to  oldest and you can see obviously the  oldest  that 90 year old group is very high  indeed i'll just put that into a  logarithmic scale so you can see the  bottom end as well  and let's just kind of go through this  so 90 year olds up there pre-vaccination  60 year olds for instance  pre-vaccination  are down there but if we reduce those  bars in line with what those  pharmaceutical companies say they should  be reduced by  that they go down the risk of dying  across the piece goes down but  even so even if they're working  supposedly as they should do  the risk for a 90 year old is still in  line with a 60 year old  pre-vaccination so it's not eliminating  it but it is reducing it  second thing is this just look at how  many people have been vaccinated  of that pool that we're talking about so  these are people who've got delta you  can see that about 85 percent or so  were vaccinated so that's most of your  sample pool and then when you look at  other things like hospitalizations  those blue bars the blue bit of the bar  is bigger than the red bit  but now break it down look at how many  of those people who were vaccinated went  on to hospital it's about 3.5 percent  now look at how much of the red bit so  those who are unvaccinated  were hospitalized 8.4 you see  there's a difference a kind of  difference in likelihood 2.4 times more  hospitalizations per case among those  who are  unvaccinated and yet the sheer number of  those who  are hospitalized having been vaccinated  is higher  similar thing when we look at deaths as  well so the same thing again we start  with total number of cases  then we look at the number of deaths and  then we look at how many deaths  per case and for vaccinated people it's  two percent of those who are  tested positive a delta went on to die  for unvaccinated  it's 5.6 of those uh who got the disease  went on to die so a higher proportion  again  2.8 times more deaths per case and yet  the sheer number of those who have  vaccinated who went on to die was  greater than the number who unvaccinated  just underlines that simple numbers on  their own  don't tell the full story
 

